{%- comment -%}
PFC Back on Track — every stated intention that has stopped moving, plus the
smallest step back in. One recovery surface across the intention layers:
Current Focus (quarter) · projects (months) · habits (daily + monthly reps).
Replaces the retired slipping screen. Standalone tasks are excluded on
purpose — task recovery is the 2+1's job.

Worst first everywhere: RED focus above YELLOW, longest-idle projects first,
biggest habit gap first. Every focus/project row carries its re-entry step
(the landing anchor / next task) because the step is the start trigger.

An empty screen is a GOOD state and must read as one ("ALL ON TRACK").

E-ink rules: no emoji, no inline styles — framework classes only. Status is
the colour spelled out (RED / YELLOW), one vocabulary across every screen.
{%- endcomment -%}
